      "note": "Microtubule v5H (nnU-Net ResEnc-M + curvature-bounded instancer). Measured 2026-08-17 on an A5000: 4.0-4.4 s for a 1024x1024 frame carrying 65 microtubules, and 0.73 GiB peak VRAM -- FLAT at 2048x2048, because the network tiles at 512x512 instead of running a ViT over the whole frame. The 1500 MB here is that peak plus headroom for the CUDA context. Runtime is dominated by the single-threaded numpy instancer, so it scales with MT count rather than frame area. Batch size pinned to 1 -- frame-parallelism happens upstream via the queue. These numbers are SERVED over GET /api/v1/models and are what a VRAM-budget decision reads; the previous entry still described v7 (DINOv3-L + PySOAX, 6500 MB)."
