      "note": "Neurite/soma (nnU-Net v2 ResEnc-M, 2D, 3-fold logit-space ensemble, 3 classes). Measured 2026-08-28 on an A5000 with the live service already holding ~8.5 GB, across two runs at different card load: 2.5-4.0 s for 1024x1024, 12.9-14.9 s for 2048x2048, 132-150 s for the 6657x6664 frames it was trained on. Runtime is dominated by forward passes and scales with tile count, not content: a 1024x1024 frame is 9 tiles x 3 folds x 4 mirror variants = 108 passes of 512x512. VRAM: 1.70 GiB reserved for the three resident fold networks plus a per-call working set sized by the FRAME (the two fp16 accumulators are C x H x W) -- 3.35 GiB peak reserved on the 6657x6664 frame, ~2.2 GiB on 2048x2048; the 4000 MB here is the former plus the CUDA context. Batch size pinned to 1: batching would multiply the frame-sized accumulators, and frame-parallelism happens upstream via the queue. expected_throughput is the 1024x1024 figure (0.25 img/s); on native-resolution frames it is 0.0076. These numbers are SERVED over GET /api/v1/models and are what a VRAM-budget decision reads."
    }
